From 511ecdb2348f21d8f32e2b3a0572798eb744b9d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SkillBuddy Agent <agent@skillbuddy.local>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 10:01:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Critical bug fixes from live testing: hooks crash, filter
 sheet regressions, styled popups
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- FIXED CRASH: 'Rendered more hooks than during previous render' when
  opening a job card. Root cause: a useMemo (sortedForAll) was declared
  AFTER the screenLoading/job-not-found early returns in the Bidding
  Dashboard, so it was skipped on the first render and called on the
  second — a genuine Rules-of-Hooks violation. Moved it above all early
  returns.

- FIXED REGRESSION: the filter bottom sheet's dimmed backdrop was
  showing solid opaque background instead of the previous screen
  showing through. Root cause: the global Stack contentStyle background
  fix (previous commit) was being inherited by the filter route's
  transparentModal presentation, which needs contentStyle: transparent
  specifically. Added a per-screen override.

- FIXED FAKE UI: the Price Range 'slider' was a purely decorative View
  with no thumbs and no touch handling at all — confirmed by testing,
  matches the reported 'no balls to drag' bug. Built a real RangeSlider
  component with two draggable PanResponder-driven thumbs, wired into
  the filter sheet with live min/max values.

- Replaced default unstyled Alert.alert popups with a new app-styled
  AlertModalContext (blurred backdrop, themed card, icon, proper
  button styling matching the rest of the app) — applied to Booking
  Confirmed, Cancel Job, Accept Bid, Cancel Bid, and invalid-bid-price
  alerts.

- Renamed the mock user identity from 'Alex Johnson' to 'Marta Ozola'
  (name/email/username) — the greeting binding itself was already
  correctly wired everywhere in a prior pass; the visible complaint was
  the placeholder-like mock value itself.

Full typecheck (skillbuddy + libs): zero errors.

Remaining from this testing round, not yet addressed (follow-up pass):
Service Detail screen visual/UX overhaul with a scrolling (non-sticky)
image header, directional back/forward navigation animations, deeper
header polish pass, and the requested per-tab icon morph animations
(door/blocks/briefcase/chat/eyes).
